                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fb6332d-7c51-4302-98f2-0da7ecf9f2a9",
                                                "sense_id": "d7782603-7d72-38fb-8811-619846dc3400",
                                                "text": "We had to have a young lady assistant to help us work this graft; and I asked Buck if he knew of one to fill the bill.\n\"One,\" says I, \"that is cool and wise and strictly business from her pompadour to her Oxfords. No ex-toe-dancers or gum-chewers or crayon portrait canvassers for this.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81437993-aca6-3632-96e4-0f3f50a0110d",
                                        "entry_id": "af9369c2-cfba-3e26-97b4-87bed2e76da9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of basket weave cotton fabric used for clothing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "attributive",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "165f2feb-4983-4976-87e8-2bae0665443d",
                                                "sense_id": "81437993-aca6-3632-96e4-0f3f50a0110d",
                                                "text": "I was amazed at the sight of such a medley of things. The newest shapes in straw hats were lying side by side with camp ovens and frying-pans, while flannel and Oxford shirts, together with wideawake felt hats, vests, collars, and ties, kept company with boxes of tea, bags of flour, and ready-tapped barrels of whiskey, rum, and gin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
